 222:                 so they are held, all at once with bits 5-7, by `rb t2ctl b27' / `rb t1ctl
 223:                 b27' (measured: `&& !(reg & COVF)' 188/190).  Those two rows REST ON A FILED
 224:                 DEFECT and must be re-cut when it is fixed (bits 4-7 via overflows; bits 2-3
