 236:                 (the T1/T2 label: `rb t1icr', `op t1icr dcl', `pend1 *' hold the T1 value,
 237:                 every T2 row the other).
 238:                 TxCTL reads relative_addr too, as its RMW index: the same T1/T2 rows.
 239:                 BIT COVERAGE, the checkable form of the above (pass 9, Opus seat): reg[TxCTL]
 240:                 is held at {0x00, 0x03, 0x11, 0x81 (masked to bit 7 and CEN: the masked rows' KILL channel
 241:                 is CEN alone -- a landed write drives idata 0 and clears it -- bit 7 is arming, and
 242:                 bits 1-6 of that state are pinned only by `ovf*' at the exact 0x11, so the ovfhi wide
 243:                 writes must keep bit 0 clear; Opus, pass 10), 0xfc} -- all eight bits held SET and CLEAR;
