 245:                 ways, bits 3, 6, 7 dead by census.  That is why every single-bit predicate on
 246:                 either register is killed, and it is what a future edit must preserve; the
 247:                 pending counts are held at 0, 1 and thousands.
 248:                 JOINT CELLS.  The rule (pass 10, the flagship seat; BOUNDED on pass 11 by the same
 249:                 seat against its own letter; CLAUDE.md clause (d)): a joint cell is ENUMERATED when
 250:                 the guarded body's own code distinguishes it, and the FLOOR -- the cells a row is
