 252:                 device-STATE lvalues the fix's own repair path reads that are jointly reachable
 253:                 through its own data flow.  Here that is {T2, T1} x {p1 = 0, > 0} x {p2 = 0, > 0}:
 254:                 one pcc_timer_tick callback increments both counts and reassert_interrupts reads
 255:                 both, so (p1, p2) is a joint input of the model.  EIGHT floor cells, every one held
 256:                 at a wide write: (T2, 0, 0) by `latch all' (0x0003) and `rb t2icr' (0xaab8), (T1, 0, 0) by `op t1icr dcl' (0x0303) and `rb t1icr' -- NOT `latch all', which iterates BLOCKS12 at 0x1a and never writes T1ICR (Opus, pass 11); (T1, >0, 0) `pend1 rb'; (T2, >0,
 257:                 0) `pend1 rb2'; (T2, 0, >0) `pend2 rb'; (T1, 0, >0) `pend2 rb1'; (T2, >0, >0)
 258:                 `pendboth rb'; (T1, >0, >0) `pendboth rb1'.  PLUS TWO, pass 13 -- the INT axis, which the
 259:                 pass-11 enumeration dismissed as derived from the count: an IEN-clear byte write zeroes
